WrapperToken::setPauser
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
└── when caller is owner
    ├── when pauser is zero address
    │   └── it should set pauser status and emit PauserUpdated
    ├── when pauser is non-zero address
    │   ├── when pauseType is zero
    │   │   ├── when status is false
    │   │   │   └── it should remove pauser status and emit PauserUpdated
    │   │   └── when status is true
    │   │       └── it should set pauser status and emit PauserUpdated
    │   └── when pauseType is non-zero
    │       ├── when status is false
    │       │   └── it should remove pauser status and emit PauserUpdated
    │       └── when status is true
    │           └── it should set pauser status and emit PauserUpdated
    └── when pauser already has status
        ├── when changing from true to false
        │   └── it should update status and emit PauserUpdated
        └── when changing from false to true
            └── it should update status and emit PauserUpdated
